# Maintain docs/

`docs/` is operational truth. README is a product overview only.

When a change adds or alters a route, env var, Docker flag, or user-visible flow, update the matching file in the same change:

- routes, handlers, URL prefixes → [docs/routes.md](docs/routes.md)
- env vars, how to run, Docker socket → [docs/running.md](docs/running.md)
- process layout, proxy, container model → [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md)
- index links if you add a new docs file → [docs/README.md](docs/README.md)

```text
# BAD: new POST /admin/workspaces/{id}/restart, docs/routes.md unchanged
# GOOD: handler and docs/routes.md land together
```

Do not document unimplemented features. Do not copy operational tables into README.md.
